    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Walk the Line (2005) revolutionized the musical biopic through Joaquin Phoenix's raw portrayal of Johnny Cash and Reese Witherspoon's Oscar-winning turn as June Carter. Unlike sanitized predecessors, director James Mangold dives deep into Cash's darkness - his pill addiction, failed first marriage, and crushing guilt over his brother's death. The film's power comes from showing how June's love and music literally saved Johnny's life. It set a new standard for music biopics, directly influencing later hits like <a href=\"/movie/1677\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1677\">Ray</a> (2004) and <a href=\"/movie/424694\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"424694\">Bohemian Rhapsody</a> (2018)."
      },
      {
